Z||000016||pherder||02-10-2000||04:41 PM||||I had a shift gate in my Ferrari 308 kit car.<P>If you plan on shifting your car in a hurry ... don't bother putting a shift gate in.  Unless you take it slow and make sure you are putting it into the hole where the gear is, you will hit the "gate" every time and miss the shift!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>That was one of the most distressing things about driving that 308!<P>Look good?  YES!!  Work well ... NO!<P>Paul||||reg||13
Z||000017||TOM||02-11-2000||12:29 AM||||HEY LENNY. First off the are counter bored not counter sunk. And stainless is real hard to work with. And hard on the cutters and drills. And hard to get a killer finish||||reg||1
